      "id": "startup-policy-and-tool-publication",
      "title": "Startup policy fixes the published capability surface",
      "classification": "enforced",
      "actor": "Roslyn Workbench Host",
      "outcome": "The startup-selected operational mode resolves to immutable policy primitives, and only tools permitted by that effective policy are published.",
      "boundary": "Enforcement begins during Host composition and applies to the built-in tools published by that process. MCP requests cannot widen the startup policy.",
      "residualRisk": "An authorised operator can restart the Host with different settings. External plugin code runs within the separately documented plugin boundary.",
