      "id": "durable-recovery",
      "title": "Interrupted persistence retains versioned recovery evidence",
      "classification": "enforced",
      "actor": "Roslyn Workbench commit and recovery services",
      "outcome": "Commit persistence uses versioned durable evidence, reports unfinished states, and preserves unsupported versions rather than guessing how to recover them.",
      "boundary": "The guarantee covers recovery artifacts created and read by Roslyn Workbench in its configured state directory.",
      "residualRisk": "Operating-system or storage failure can still make evidence incomplete; status reports that condition for manual resolution.",
